  ('7761a3d1-7339-5f00-9da2-403cf2d4ae5f', null, (select id from public.skills where slug = 'read-g12-word-parts'), null, 'medium',
   $q$The prefix im- means "not," percept relates to "noticing with the senses," and the suffix -ible means "able to be." What is an "imperceptible" shimmer?$q$, $q$[{"text":"A shimmer so faint it can hardly be noticed","is_correct":true},{"text":"A shimmer that disappears forever after rain","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"overstates-meaning"},{"text":"A shimmer that only scientists' tools can record","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"too-narrow"},{"text":"A shimmer bright enough to notice easily","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"ignores-prefix"}]$q$::jsonb, $q$A shimmer so faint it can hardly be noticed$q$, $q$Im plus percept plus ible means not able to be noticed, and the passage pairs it with "almost" and "dimmed" to describe a nearly invisible glow. Ignoring the prefix im- gives the opposite meaning, bright and obvious.$q$, 'draft', 'e3c23a21-e91e-5e9a-bdfa-606154d2af13')
