   $q$The root phon means "sound," and the suffix -etic means "relating to." What were Marisol's "phonetic" labels?$q$, $q$[{"text":"Labels that named each problem by how it sounded","is_correct":true},{"text":"Labels written in standard musical notation","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"too-narrow"},{"text":"Labels that ranked each pipe by its size","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"ignores-root-clues"},{"text":"Labels recorded on a telephone for later use","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"literal-reading"}]$q$::jsonb, $q$Labels that named each problem by how it sounded$q$, $q$Phonetic labels relate to sound, and her examples, "hiss," "buzz," and "the cough," each imitate or describe a noise. Musical notation records pitches, which is not what her invented labels did.$q$, 'draft', 'ee47fb45-ac2b-5a47-a651-efdc0d8c5d75')
