  ('629b68fe-efa7-597e-81fa-c04899ad6ad8', null, (select id from public.skills where slug = 'read-g12-word-parts'), null, 'easy',
   $q$The root rupt means "to break." What is a "corrupted" bit in the passage?$q$, $q$[{"text":"A piece of data that has been damaged and is no longer reliable","is_correct":true},{"text":"A piece of data that has been copied many times over","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"context-only-guess"},{"text":"A piece of data that was deleted on purpose by engineers","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"unsupported-inference"},{"text":"A piece of data that arrives faster than the others","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"ignores-root-clues"}]$q$::jsonb, $q$A piece of data that has been damaged and is no longer reliable$q$, $q$Rupt signals breaking, and the passage says a corrupted bit can turn a photograph "into a streaked, unreadable image." Nothing suggests engineers removed data on purpose; the damage comes from radiation and noise.$q$, 'draft', '522d847e-ee97-58b3-95a7-1ab8533b8011')
