   $q$The root err means "to wander," and the suffix -atic means "tending to." What does it mean when a reading seems "erratic"?$q$, $q$[{"text":"It rises slowly and steadily each hour","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"ignores-root-clues"},{"text":"It cannot be received on Earth at all","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"overstates-meaning"},{"text":"It stays exactly the same over time","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"opposite-meaning"},{"text":"It changes irregularly and unpredictably","is_correct":true}]$q$::jsonb, $q$It changes irregularly and unpredictably$q$, $q$Erratic means tending to wander, and the passage explains it right away as "jumping wildly from one moment to the next." A slow, steady rise is the kind of orderly change erratic rules out.$q$, 'draft', '522d847e-ee97-58b3-95a7-1ab8533b8011')
