   $q$The root vor means "to eat," and the suffix -acious means "tending to" or "full of." What does "voracious" suggest about the birds in the late afternoon?$q$, $q$[{"text":"They share their food with others","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"confuses-related-idea"},{"text":"They eat slowly and carefully","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"opposite-meaning"},{"text":"They stop eating to save energy","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"ignores-root-clues"},{"text":"They eat eagerly and in large amounts","is_correct":true}]$q$::jsonb, $q$They eat eagerly and in large amounts$q$, $q$Voracious means having a great appetite, and the birds are "gulping food as fast as they can before darkness falls." Eating slowly and carefully is the opposite of that hurried gulping.$q$, 'draft', '0d56c0a4-d8a4-525e-bc7d-64be0afa701d')
