   $q$"Circadian" comes from circa ("about") and dies ("day"). Which statement from the passage best shows what a "circadian pattern" is?$q$, $q$[{"text":"Visits peak after sunrise, dip at midday, and rise again before sunset","is_correct":true},{"text":"Mixed flocks travel together during the coldest weeks","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"confuses-time-scale"},{"text":"Birds circle the feeder several times before landing to eat","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"spelling-coincidence"},{"text":"Chickadees take one seed at a time to a nearby branch","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"unrelated-detail"}]$q$::jsonb, $q$Visits peak after sunrise, dip at midday, and rise again before sunset$q$, $q$A circadian pattern repeats on a roughly daily cycle, and the passage describes a "daily rhythm" from sunrise to sunset. Circling the feeder relies on the look of "circa," not its meaning, and the passage never mentions it.$q$, 'draft', '0d56c0a4-d8a4-525e-bc7d-64be0afa701d')
